            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FOR10" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Elias</forename>
                        <surname>Fordham</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000-01-01">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>Farmer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> This seems to be Elias Fordham of Cambridgeshire, but also of Royston,
                            Herts. Ed Pope points towards a connection to Henry Crabve Robinson,
                            through being witnesses to his brothers marriage. There is
                            correspondence with Forham in the AAbinger collection - relating to
                            Godwin giving an account, in November 1811,of what he sees as the
                            different characters of Fanny and Mary Godwin. There is also a letter
                            in 1822 commenting on a poem/tragedy written by Fordham. </p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
